    <HELP>**The most overloaded table in the system.** One row can be any or all of: a login account, a business contact, an employee, a reporting-tool user and a correspondence actor. Ten windows are built on it - User Management, Employee Master, Representative Info, Prospect, Business Partner, Channel Partner, Customer Master, Vendor Master, User Substitute and SSO Data Mapping - and most fields are only meaningful on some of them. The login side carries the password, the two-factor settings, the authentication tokens, the failed login count and the PIN and card used at a till. The employee side carries joining and relieving dates, qualifications with percentages and years, blood group and statutory identifiers. The contact side carries the address, greeting, telephone numbers and opt-out. **A query about people has to establish which population it means**, because `AD_User` holds employees and customers' staff in the same table. Note also that HR identity is conventionally taken from `C_BPartner` rather than from here; this table is the account and contact record.</HELP>
